## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/glow.html
- Summary (EN): Glow adds a glow effect to an input layer, usually an image, by finding its bright regions. It is useful for effects such as neon lighting and explosions.
- Résumé (FR) : Glow ajoute une lueur aux zones les plus claires d'un calque, selon un seuil de luminance réglable.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer that receives the glow", "mask: optional per-pixel mask, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the new glow value mixes with the original (default 1)", "Glow Threshold: luminance above which pixels receive glow (default 0.75)", "Output Glow Only: outputs only the glow, for use as an AOV or in a Blend COP", "Brightness: brightness and spread of the glow (default 2)", "Saturation: colour intensity of the glow (default 1)", "Tint: colour applied to the glow (default 1, 1, 1)", "Filter: Gaussian (default) or Box blur used in the subnetwork", "Units: Image (default) or Pixels as the blur radius unit", "Size: blur radius in the chosen units (default 0.05 for Image, 3 for Pixels)", "Scale Size: anisotropic scaling of the glow size"]

- Caveats: ["The blur comes from Blur COPs inside the subnetwork, so softness is controlled indirectly through Units, Size, Filter and Scale Size", "The page mentions an Aspect parameter while the parameter list shows Scale Size; the page does not clarify the difference", "Only high-luminance areas glow, so Glow Threshold strongly drives the result", "No performance characteristics are described"]

